# trivyignore-template: v1 — ships WITH nightly.yml (its trivy job passes
# `trivyignores: .trivyignore`, and trivy treats a MISSING ignore file as a
# FATAL flag error, not an empty list — so a repo that copies the workflow
# without this file has a Trivy job that has NEVER SCANNED ANYTHING, red on
# a flag error with its real findings hidden behind it. Measured: go-enclave
# 2026-08-26, ten HIGH x/crypto CVEs sat behind the FATAL for the workflow's
# whole life — go-enclave PR #5.)
#
# Source of truth: software/templates/github-actions/.trivyignore in the
# automatethethings repo. Copy to the repo ROOT (not .github/), alongside
# copying nightly.yml. Keep it EMPTY except for CVE IDs with a dated reason:
#
#   # 2026-01-01 <who>: <why this finding does not apply here>
#   CVE-XXXX-NNNNN

# 2026-10-22 agent-software (DS-3252): protobuf-java 2.6.1, shaded in AGP 9.0.0
# lint's com.android.tools.external.com-intellij:kotlin-compiler:32.0.0;
# build-only, in the image's Gradle cache, not in the APK. Remove with the bump
# to the first stable AGP 9.5, or by 2026-11-21.
CVE-2021-22569 exp:2026-11-21

